W44-51 — patches ref-frame predictor A/B (tree-learn vs libjxl-parity Gradient)
Date: 2026-05-19
Host: water-cooled AMD Ryzen 9 7950X, 128 GB RAM (single-thread)

==============================================================================
VERDICT: H3 RULED OUT — predictor choice does NOT move bytes on patches ref
frame. All 16 cells byte-identical between tree-learned `Predictor::Variable`
and forced `Predictor::Gradient`.
==============================================================================

Hypothesis (H3 from W44-48):
- libjxl unconditionally uses Predictor::Gradient for patches ref frames
  (`~/work/jxl-efforts/libjxl/lib/jxl/enc_patch_dictionary.cc:828`).
- Our default at e7+ enables tree-learned Predictor::Variable when
  `ref_w>=128 AND ref_h>=128` (`vardct/patches.rs:2921`).
- codec_wiki e7 d=3..6 ref frame is 133×130 → triggers tree-learn.
- cjxl ships +1590 patches bytes / -4600 main bytes per W44-46:
  the working theory was that denser per-pixel Gradient residuals subtract
  MORE main-AC energy, lowering main-frame bytes.
- A/B test: force `Predictor::Gradient` on ours_grad, leave tree-learn on
  ours_tree, measure byte delta.

Initial knob attempt:
- `LossyInternalParams::patch_ref_tree_learning: Some(true|false)`
  is plumbed correctly to `vardct/patches.rs::encode_reference_frame`
  (verified via eprintln probe — `use_tree_learning=true` vs `false` both
  reach the call site).
- BUT: `modular/frame.rs::encode_modular_body` always routes through
  `write_modular_stream_with_tree_dc_quant_knobs` when
  `dc_quant_custom.is_some()`, which is the case at distance > 0 (the
  patches ref frame uses libjxl-derived per-channel DC quant scales for
  d>0). The `use_tree_learning=false` flag is silently ignored at d>0.
- This makes the existing `patch_ref_tree_learning` knob non-functional
  for distance > 0 — it only flips the dispatch for the lossless
  `dc_quant_custom=None` path.

V2 fix to enable the real A/B:
- The `ours_grad` bench arm injects `ModularKnobs.modular_predictor = Some(5)`
  (Predictor::Gradient) which IS honored by
  `write_modular_stream_with_tree_dc_quant_knobs` via
  `resolve_tree_learn_force_predictor` (single-leaf `simple_tree(forced)`,
  no ID3). This skips ID3 and emits the same shape libjxl produces.

Sweep design:
- 4 gb82-sc screenshots (codec_wiki, imac_g3, terminal, windows95)
  × 4 distances {3, 4, 5, 6}
  × 3 encoders {ours_tree, ours_grad, cjxl}
  = 48 encodes.
- effort=7, threads=1, default LossyConfig (no buttloop at e7).
- Decode + score via jxl-oxide linear-sRGB (PNG-metadata immune
  per CLAUDE.md).

