Butteraugli + SSIM2: also bit-identical between tree/grad on every cell
(deltas confirm decoded pixels are exactly the same, not just byte-equal).

Probe trace (from W44-51 instrumented run):
  PROBE: encode_reference_frame d=3 ref=133x130
         use_tree_learning=true  enable_tree=true  force_pred=None
  PROBE: encode_reference_frame d=3 ref=133x130
         use_tree_learning=false enable_tree=false force_pred=Some(5)
(ref frame is 133×130 on codec_wiki — meets the >=128 threshold, so
tree-learn would fire in production. Forcing Gradient via Some(5)
produces the SAME bytes as ID3-learned Variable.)

Conclusion (H3 RULED OUT):
- ID3 tree learning on packed-patches ref frames (RCT + Gradient candidates
  across small windows of glyphs) converges to the same per-leaf prediction
  as a fixed Gradient predictor. The single-leaf `Predictor::Gradient` tree
  IS already the best fit for this content shape — no other predictor in
  the 14-predictor candidate set offers a measurable improvement on a
  133×130 RCT-decorrelated XYB image of packed patches.
- The cjxl "+1590 patches / -4600 main" delta from W44-46 is NOT from
  predictor choice. The ref frame produces literally the same bytes
  whether ID3 picks Gradient or Gradient is forced.
- This rules out the most likely H3 from W44-48's three remaining
  hypotheses. Recommend H2 (bin-packer layout — cjxl 140×132 vs ours
  133×130 admits 1-2 more patches?) or H1 (CC enumeration / BFS-DFS
  difference) as the next chunk.

Reproducer (post-revert, with knob plumbed but not effective at d>0):
```
cargo run -p jxl-encoder --release --features __expert \
    --example w44_51_refframe_predictor_ab \
    -- --output benchmarks/w44_51_refframe_predictor_ab_2026-05-19.tsv
```
The above runs the bench but ours_grad ≡ ours_tree post-revert (the knob
is a no-op at d>0). The DEFINITIVE A/B with `force_pred=Some(5)` is
recorded in this TSV; reproducing requires re-applying the V2 probe at
`vardct/patches.rs:2921` (commit `patch ref-frame ModularKnobs
modular_predictor=Some(5) when !enable_tree`).

Action taken:
- AUDIT-ONLY chunk. No production behavior change. Doc-comment added at
  `vardct/patches.rs:2920-2925` referencing W44-51 verdict, so future
  agents do not re-investigate.
- Bench TSV + meta committed.

