Sub-finding (orphan knob):
- `LossyInternalParams::patch_ref_tree_learning` (effort.rs:1790,
  effort_expert_tests.rs:259, vardct/bitstream.rs:2008/2125) does NOT
  alter bitstream at distance > 0 because the FrameEncoder dispatch in
  `modular/frame.rs::encode_modular_body:2294` routes any
  `dc_quant_custom.is_some()` path unconditionally through the tree-learn
  writer. The existing unit test (`effort_expert_tests::lossy_override_
  patch_ref_tree_learning`) passes only because it ALSO sets
  `k_info_loss_mul_base: Some(1.5)`. Recommended follow-up issue: either
  wire the knob through to the dc_quant path (requires a new
  `write_modular_stream_with_no_tree_dc_quant_knobs` variant), or remove
  the knob as dead code at d>0 since the V2 measurement shows there's no
  RD lever there anyway.
